  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「コシダ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B3%E3%82%B7%E3%83%80",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106361378,
      "text": "コシダ は、時に背が高くなるシダ植物で、乾燥した山野に密な群落を作る。ウラジロに様々な点で似ているが、葉が繰り返して二叉分枝する点で異なる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Dicranopteris linearis」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dicranopteris_linearis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1314486312,
      "text": "Dicranopteris linearis is a common species of fern known by many common names, including Old World forked fern, uluhe (Hawaiian), and dilim (Filipino). It is one of the most widely distributed ferns of the wet Old World tropics and adjacent regions, including Polynesia and the Pacific. In parts of the New World tropics its niche is filled by its relative, Dicranopteris pectinatus."
    }
  },
